Subject: [PATCH] fix(compositor): map xdg_popup surfaces

An xdg_popup can never become mapped. `Surface.mapped` is only ever set by
`FloatingDesktopSurface.commit()`, which is reached through
`DesktopSurface.commit()`. XdgToplevel, ShellSurface and XWaylandShellSurface
all call it; XdgPopup does not -- it acks the configure, schedules a render, and
returns.

The result is that a popup surface is created with the correct role, receives
its buffer, and then sits at `mapped: false` forever. It never enters the view
stack and never appears. Observed on 1.0.0-rc1 and still present on master:

    role: XdgPopup, hasBuffer: true, mapped: false, view: not in viewStack

This means no menu, dropdown, combobox or tooltip can be shown by any client,
native or web -- it is hit the first time a user right-clicks.

The fix mirrors XdgToplevel.onCommit: call `this.desktopSurface.commit()`.
`FloatingDesktopSurface.commit()` already returns early while
`surface.size === undefined`, so the bufferless first commit is unaffected.

Verified with a client that opens an xdg_popup with a real XdgPositioner: after
the change the popup maps, enters the view stack, receives a render state and a
texture, and the compositor's computed position matches the positioner's anchor
rect exactly.

--- a/packages/compositor/src/XdgPopup.ts
+++ b/packages/compositor/src/XdgPopup.ts
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@ export default class XdgPopup implements XdgPopupRequests, SurfaceRole, DesktopS
       this.xdgSurface.scheduleConfigure(false, () => this.sendConfigure())
     }
     this.committed = true
+    this.desktopSurface.commit()
     surface.session.renderer.render()
   }
 
